tags: host-name, domain, dns

A kind of network: one host name and its ports. The instance can connect to the IPv4
addresses of the name, on these ports only.

The value is key=value lines, sorted by key, separated by a newline. The key host is
required: a lowercase DNS name with at least one ".". The key port is optional: a port
from 1 to 65535. With no port, the ports are 80 and 443. Another key is not valid.
Example: host=api.example.com and port=8443, one on each line.

The node finds the members at each start: it resolves the A records of the name with
its own resolver. It does not use IPv6. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=domain
ipv6=not used
members=the IPv4 addresses of the A records of host, resolved by the node at the start, on the ports
name=host-name
port.default=80 and 443
value=key=value lines sorted by key: host (required, a lowercase DNS name with at least one '.'), port (optional, 1 to 65535); no other key
